<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <meta name="description" content="Privacy Policy for Image Compressor — an on-device Android photo compression app." />
  <title>Privacy Policy — Image Compressor</title>
  <style>
    :root {
      --bg: #f7f8fa;
      --card: #ffffff;
      --text: #1a1d26;
      --muted: #5c6370;
      --border: #e6e8ee;
      --accent: #1b6ef3;
      --accent-soft: #eaf2ff;
    }
    * { box-sizing: border-box; }
    body {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
      color: var(--text);
      background: var(--bg);
      line-height: 1.65;
      font-size: 16px;
    }
    .wrap {
      max-width: 820px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 32px 20px 64px;
    }
    header {
      background: var(--card);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 16px;
      padding: 28px 28px 24px;
      margin-bottom: 20px;
    }
    h1 {
      margin: 0 0 8px;
      font-size: 1.85rem;
      letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    }
    .meta {
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 0.95rem;
    }
    .badge {
      display: inline-block;
      margin-top: 14px;
      background: var(--accent-soft);
      color: var(--accent);
      font-weight: 600;
      font-size: 0.85rem;
      padding: 6px 10px;
      border-radius: 999px;
    }
    section {
      background: var(--card);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 16px;
      padding: 24px 28px;
      margin-bottom: 16px;
    }
    h2 {
      margin: 0 0 12px;
      font-size: 1.2rem;
      letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    }
    h3 {
      margin: 18px 0 8px;
      font-size: 1.02rem;
    }
    p, li { color: var(--text); }
    p { margin: 0 0 12px; }
    ul { margin: 0 0 12px; padding-left: 1.2rem; }
    li { margin-bottom: 6px; }
    a { color: var(--accent); }
    .muted { color: var(--muted); }
    table {
      width: 100%;
      border-collapse: collapse;
      margin: 12px 0 4px;
      font-size: 0.95rem;
    }
    th, td {
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      padding: 10px 12px;
      text-align: left;
      vertical-align: top;
    }
    th { background: #f3f5f9; }
    footer {
      margin-top: 24px;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      text-align: center;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="meta"><strong>App:</strong> Image Compressor<br />
        <strong>Developer:</strong> Moizraja09<br />
        <strong>Effective date:</strong> October 31, 2026<br />
        <strong>Last updated:</strong> October 31, 2026
      </p>
      <span class="badge">On-device processing · No account · No ads · No tracking SDKs</span>
    </header>

    <section>
      <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy explains how <strong>Image Compressor</strong> (“the App”, “we”, “us”, or “our”)
        handles information when you use the Android application published on Google Play.
      </p>
      <p>
        Image Compressor is designed as a <strong>local, offline-first utility</strong>. Photos you select are
        compressed on your device. The App does <strong>not</strong> require an account, does <strong>not</strong>
        include advertising SDKs, and does <strong>not</strong> include analytics or crash-reporting SDKs that
        would transmit your personal data to us.
      </p>
      <p class="muted">
        Please read this Policy carefully. By installing or using the App, you acknowledge the practices
        described here. If you do not agree, please uninstall and stop using the App.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>2. Who we are &amp; scope</h2>
      <p>
        This Policy applies only to the Android app <strong>Image Compressor</strong> distributed via Google Play
        under the developer account associated with this publication, and to this privacy policy webpage.
      </p>
      <p>
        It does <strong>not</strong> cover third-party websites, apps, or services you may open from the App
        (for example, your device browser when viewing this Policy, or apps you choose via the Android share sheet).
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>3. Summary (at a glance)</h2>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Topic</th>
            <th>Our practice</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Photo / image content</td>
            <td>Processed only on your device. Not uploaded to our servers.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Accounts / login</td>
            <td>Not used. No registration.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Ads / trackers</td>
            <td>Not included in the App.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Internet access by the App</td>
            <td>The App does not declare the Internet permission and does not send your photos or settings to our servers.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Local settings &amp; history</td>
            <td>Stored on your device only (see Section 5).</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Children</td>
            <td>Not directed to children under 13 (see Section 11).</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>4. Information we do <em>not</em> collect</h2>
      <p>We do <strong>not</strong> collect, receive, or store on our servers:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your photos, images, or video files</li>
        <li>EXIF / GPS / device metadata from your images</li>
        <li>Name, email, phone number, or other contact details (unless you choose to email us)</li>
        <li>Precise or approximate location for our use</li>
        <li>Advertising identifiers for advertising or analytics</li>
        <li>Payment or financial information (the App does not process payments itself)</li>
        <li>Contacts, SMS, call logs, or microphone / continuous camera capture for our services</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We do <strong>not</strong> operate a backend that receives your media for compression.
        Compression runs locally using on-device Android image processing.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>5. Information processed or stored on your device</h2>
      <p>
        The App may process or store the following <strong>on your device only</strong>, to provide App features:
      </p>

      <h3>5.1 Photos and images you select</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          You choose images using the system photo picker / media selection UI (for example, gallery or camera
          capture flows provided by Android or OEM apps).
        </li>
        <li>
          Selected image content is read temporarily so the App can compress it to your chosen target size and format
          (such as JPEG or WebP).
        </li>
        <li>
          Processing happens in device memory / local temporary files as needed to create the compressed output.
        </li>
        <li>
          We do not upload those images to our servers.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>5.2 Optional EXIF / metadata stripping</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          The App can remove EXIF and related metadata (which may include GPS location, device model, and similar tags)
          from the <strong>output</strong> image when you enable that option.
        </li>
        <li>
          This feature is intended to help you reduce file size and avoid sharing sensitive metadata in the saved/shared file.
        </li>
        <li>
          Metadata stripping is performed on-device. We do not transmit EXIF data to ourselves.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>5.3 Compressed output files</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Compressed files may be kept in the App’s local app storage for history/preview features.
        </li>
        <li>
          If you use <strong>Save</strong>, the App may write the output into your device gallery under a folder such as
          <code>Pictures/ImageCompressor</code> via Android MediaStore APIs.
        </li>
        <li>
          Saved gallery files remain under your control on the device (and any cloud backup you personally enable for photos
          at the system or OEM level).
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>5.4 Compression history (local)</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          The App may store a limited local history (for example: file name, local file path, original/output sizes,
          format, and timestamp) so you can revisit recent compressions.
        </li>
        <li>
          History is stored in on-device preferences / local storage and is not sent to us.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>5.5 App preferences (local)</h3>
      <p>The App stores settings on your device, such as:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Preferred language</li>
        <li>Theme (system / light / dark)</li>
        <li>Default target size and output format</li>
        <li>Default EXIF-stripping preference</li>
        <li>Onboarding completion state</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>5.6 Sharing</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          If you tap Share, Android’s system share sheet lets you send the output file to an app <strong>you</strong> select
          (messaging, email, drive apps, etc.).
        </li>
        <li>
          Those third-party apps have their own privacy policies. We do not control what they do after you share.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>6. Permissions and device access</h2>
      <p>Depending on your Android version, the App may rely on the following access patterns:</p>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Access</th>
            <th>Purpose</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Photo / media selection (system picker)</td>
            <td>Let you choose the image to compress. On modern Android versions this is typically scoped selection rather than broad gallery access.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Write to shared storage / MediaStore</td>
            <td>Save compressed images to your Pictures folder when you request Save. On older Android versions (API 28 and below), a write-storage permission may be required.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>FileProvider (local sharing)</td>
            <td>Temporarily grant another app you choose read access to a compressed file during Share.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>
        The App does <strong>not</strong> request permission to access your contacts, SMS, microphone, or precise location
        for our services. Location data may exist inside an image’s EXIF tags; if present, it is processed only locally
        and can be removed from the output when EXIF stripping is enabled.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>7. How we use information</h2>
      <p>On-device data is used solely to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Compress images to your selected size/format</li>
        <li>Optionally strip metadata from outputs</li>
        <li>Save or share files at your request</li>
        <li>Show local history and remember your settings</li>
        <li>Provide language and theme preferences</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not sell personal information. We do not use your photos for advertising, profiling, or training remote AI models.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>8. Internet use &amp; opening this Privacy Policy</h2>
      <p>
        Image Compressor is built to work without sending your photos to a developer-operated server.
        The App does not declare Android Internet permission for uploading media to us.
      </p>
      <p>
        When you open <strong>Privacy Policy</strong> in Settings, the App may launch your device’s browser
        (or another HTTPS-capable viewer) to display this webpage. That browser session is handled by your
        browser/OS and may involve normal web networking outside the App process.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>9. Data sharing</h2>
      <p>We do not sell, rent, or trade your personal information.</p>
      <p>Data leaves your device through the App only when <strong>you</strong> initiate an action, such as:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Sharing a compressed file to another app you choose</li>
        <li>Saving a file to shared storage that you later sync with your own cloud backup (Google Photos, OEM gallery backup, etc.)</li>
        <li>Opening this Privacy Policy in a browser</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Google Play and your device manufacturer may independently process install, integrity, or store-related
        information under their own policies when you download or update apps from Google Play. That processing
        is governed by Google’s / OEM policies, not by a developer server operated by Image Compressor.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>10. Data retention &amp; deletion</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Temporary processing data:</strong> used during compression and not kept beyond what is needed to produce the result and support App features.</li>
        <li><strong>Local history / preferences:</strong> remain on the device until you clear App data, uninstall the App, or use in-app controls that remove history (where available).</li>
        <li><strong>Gallery saves:</strong> files you save to Pictures remain until you delete them using your gallery/file manager.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Because we do not host your photos on our servers, there is no cloud copy of your images for us to delete.
        Uninstalling the App removes App-private storage; shared gallery files you previously saved may remain until you delete them.
      </p>
      <p class="muted">
        Note: If Android Backup / device transfer features are enabled on your phone, the operating system may back up
        certain app data according to your device settings. That is controlled by Android / your Google account settings.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>11. Children’s privacy</h2>
      <p>
        The App is a general-purpose utility and is <strong>not directed to children under 13</strong>
        (or the equivalent minimum age in your jurisdiction). We do not knowingly collect personal information
        from children. If you believe a child has provided personal information to us through email contact,
        please contact us and we will delete that correspondence where applicable.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>12. Security</h2>
      <p>
        We design the App to keep sensitive media on-device. No method of electronic storage is 100% secure.
        You are responsible for protecting access to your device (screen lock, OS updates) and for reviewing
        permissions you grant.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>13. International users</h2>
      <p>
        The App processes data locally on your device wherever you use it. Because we do not operate a media
        upload backend for this App, we do not transfer your photos to developer-operated servers in other countries.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>14. Your choices &amp; controls</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Choose whether to select, compress, save, or share any image.</li>
        <li>Enable or disable EXIF/metadata stripping for outputs.</li>
        <li>Change language, theme, and default compression preferences in Settings.</li>
        <li>Clear App storage / cache or uninstall the App via Android system settings.</li>
        <li>Delete saved outputs from your gallery.</li>
        <li>Revoke permissions in Android Settings if your OS version exposed optional storage permissions.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>15. Google Play Data safety disclosures</h2>
      <p>
        In Google Play Console, Data safety answers for this App are intended to reflect that:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Photo and video / image files are processed on-device to provide App functionality</li>
        <li>Such files are not collected by the developer to a developer server</li>
        <li>No account data is collected</li>
        <li>No advertising or analytics SDK collection is performed by the App as described in this Policy</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Always treat the Play Console Data safety form as a living disclosure: if the App’s behavior changes in a future update
        (for example, adding cloud sync, ads, or analytics), this Policy and the Data safety form will be updated before or with that change.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>16. Third-party services</h2>
      <p>As of the effective date above, the App does not integrate third-party advertising, analytics, crash, or social login SDKs.</p>
      <p>
        Platform services (Android OS, Google Play, OEM gallery/camera apps, and apps you share to) are governed by their own terms and privacy policies.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>17. Changes to this Policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy to reflect App changes, legal requirements, or clarifications.
        The “Last updated” date at the top will change when we do. Material changes will be reflected on this page.
        Continued use of the App after an update means you acknowledge the revised Policy.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>18. Contact us</h2>
      <p>
        If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or the App’s privacy practices, contact the developer:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          GitHub (privacy policy repository):
          <a href="https://github.com/Moizraja09/app-privacy-policies" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            github.com/Moizraja09/app-privacy-policies
          </a>
        </li>
        <li>
          GitHub profile:
          <a href="https://github.com/Moizraja09" rel="noopener noreferrer">github.com/Moizraja09</a>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="muted">
        For the fastest response about this Policy, open an Issue on the privacy-policy repository and include
        “Image Compressor Privacy” in the title.
      </p>
    </section>

    <footer>
      © 2026 Image Compressor · On-device image compression for Android
    </footer>
  </div>
</body>
</html>

